{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Vd5Vt8QpdEQSA997iZo2j7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `auth` service is fully implemented and all 13 pre-written tests pass.\n\n## What I built\n\n**gRPC contract** — `proto/v1/auth.proto`: package `auth.v1`, service `AuthService`, the `authv1` go_package option, and exactly the 5 RPCs from the spec (`Register`, `Login`, `VerifyToken`, `Refresh`, `Logout`) with request/response messages matching the spec shapes.\n\n**Service** — `internal/server/server.go`: in-memory `Server` with `NewServer()` constructor. Behavior per the spec:\n- Users in a map keyed by email, storing a salted **SHA-256** hash (never plaintext); all users get the `guest` scope.\n- Access tokens are stateless **HMAC-SHA256 JWTs** signed with `AUTH_JWT_SECRET` (dev default if unset), claims = subject/scope/iat/exp. `VerifyToken` checks signature + expiry only, no store lookup.\n- Refresh tokens are opaque random strings held in a `sessions` map; `Refresh` mints a new access token, `Logout` deletes the session (idempotent — unknown tokens still succeed).\n- Error codes match `error_semantics` exactly: `InvalidArgument` (empty fields), `AlreadyExists` (dup register), `Unauthenticated` (bad creds / bad token / unknown-or-revoked refresh).\n\n**Entrypoint** — `cmd/auth/main.go`: gRPC on `:50051`, `/healthz`→200 on `:8080`, stdlib `log`, SIGTERM graceful shutdown, and a `//go:generate protoc …` directive.\n\n**Build/deploy** — `Makefile` (`build`/`test`/`image`; leaf-service `docker build -t agentbench/auth:dev .` since `dependent_interface` is `[]`) and a multi-stage `Dockerfile` ending in `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12`, exposing `50051`/`8080`.\n\n## Verification\n- `go generate`, `go build`, `go vet` clean; `gofmt` clean.\n- `go test ./...` → **ok** (all tests pass).\n\nTwo environment notes (not issues with the service):\n- The repo `go.work` lists sibling services (booking, payment, …) not present in this checkout, so bare `go`/`make` fails to load the workspace. I built/tested with `GOWORK=off`; in the full repo the workspace resolves normally.\n- **Docker isn't installed in this sandbox**, so I couldn't execute the image build/`/healthz` check here. The Dockerfile copies the committed generated stubs and builds `./cmd/auth`, with no `go.work` in the service-dir build context."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":894,"cache_read_input_tokens":44342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":894},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bc9541c-fba5-42cf-ac81-69a543e94cfc","uuid":"6664ea64-2e36-49e4-b788-3512d6e524f6","request_id":"req_011CbpsmPusCXgt3AeK6ApKP"}
